 "description": "Plain 1890s bolt-action service rifle, side view, horizontal, muzzle to the right. A prop for SOLDIERS to hold (across the lap, shouldered upright, or at port-arms by rotating it); never aimed at an animal, no flash, no smoke, no scope. Brown wood stock and fore-end #8a5a2e with grain strokes, grey steel barrel and receiver #4a4f55 with a light top edge, small bolt knob, trigger guard, dark butt plate. Anchor (0,0) = centre of the fore-end. Key points: rear hand on the wrist (-90,-6), front hand on the fore-end (+50,-10), muzzle (+180,-14), butt plate (-182,+2). bbox x -184..+182, y -48..+28 (about 366 long: sized against stick_man_sitting at the same scale, so a seated man's lap holds it with both ends showing).",
